### [New ebook store: original Go books from Japan…](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/2015/01/12/new-ebook-store-original-go-books-from-japan/)

Posted by [LinuxGooo](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/author/linuxgooo/ "View all posts by LinuxGooo")⋅January 12, 2015⋅ [1 Comment](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/2015/01/12/new-ebook-store-original-go-books-from-japan/#comments)

[![420812_372176399530062_768427126_n](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/420812_372176399530062_768427126_n.jpg?w=367&h=205)](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/420812_372176399530062_768427126_n.jpg)

…seen at [Art and GO @ Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/artandgogame) (Source: [Thailand Go Club](https://www.facebook.com/ThailandGoClub))

Many Go players I know love this ancient game because of the Asian culture which can be experienced herewith. – Same I like to feel the Asian spirit and traditions embedded in modernity of 21st century by playing Go and being in contact with the international GO scene.

In Western world we depend on sources for our Go studies with translations of the original Japanse, Chinese or Korean publishers. Some few Go books have been written directly in English; mostly the Go literature is translated from books being written by Chinese, Japanese or Korean high Pro Dans .

On my own yet I haven’t bought an original Japanese book lacking of language skills… as beginner mostly I use the standard books in English as I was adviced by my Go friends and teachers to study with. You find more details about on the Go wiki SL ( [Sensei’s Library](http://senseis.xmp.net/?GoBooks)), e.g. …

- **[Grade Go Problems for Beginners](http://senseis.xmp.net/?GradedGoProblemsForBeginners)**(Vol 1-4) written by Japanse [Kano Yoshinori](http://senseis.xmp.net/?KanoYoshinori)
- [**Fundamental Principles of Go**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?FundamentalPrinciplesOfGo) written by [Yilun Yang](http://senseis.xmp.net/?YilunYang)
- **[Elementary Go Series](http://senseis.xmp.net/?ElementaryGoSeries)** (Vol. 1-7) written by Japanse [Tomoko Ogawa](http://senseis.xmp.net/?TomokoOgawa) and [James Davies](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JamesDavies)
- **[Learn to Play Go series](http://senseis.xmp.net/?LearnToPlayGoSeries)** written by [Janice Kim](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JaniceKim) and [Jeong Soo-hyun](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JeongSooHyun)
- [**Level Up!**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?LevelUp) (series of Korean work books) written by Lee Jae-Hwan and supervised by [Yoo Chang-Hyuk](http://senseis.xmp.net/?YooChangHyuk) (9 PD)
- [**Basic Techniques of GO**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?BasicTechniquesOfGo) written by [Haruyama Isamu](http://senseis.xmp.net/?HaruyamaIsamu) and [Nagahara Yoshiaki](http://senseis.xmp.net/?NagaharaYoshiaki)
- [**Lessons in the Fundamentals of Go**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?LessonsInTheFundamentalsOfGo) ( _Ama to Puro) written_ by Japanese [Kageyama Toshiro](http://senseis.xmp.net/?KageyamaToshiro)
- [**Strategic Fundamentals in Go**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?StrategicFundamentalsInGo) ( _Weiqi Zhanli)_ by Chinese _[Guo Tisheng](http://senseis.xmp.net/?GuoTisheng) and Lu Wen_
- [**The Power of the Star-Point**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?Takagawa) (sub title: _The Sanrensei Opening)_ translated by [John Power](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JohnPower) (origin: [Takagawa Kaku](http://senseis.xmp.net/?Takagawa)‘s book _Sanrensei no Iryoku)_

_Further I use:_

- [**Kogo’s Joseki Dictionary**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?KogosJosekiDictionary) ( [joseki](http://senseis.xmp.net/?Joseki) encyclopedia in [SGF format](http://senseis.xmp.net/?SGFFile)) by [Alexander Dinerchtein](http://senseis.xmp.net/?AlexanderDinerchtein)

_These book titles are on my “to-do/wish list”:_

- **[Get Strong at Go Series](http://senseis.xmp.net/?GetStrongAtGoSeries)** by [Richard Bozulich](http://senseis.xmp.net/?RichardBozulich) and [Furuyama Kazunari](http://senseis.xmp.net/?FuruyamaKazunari)
- **[First Fundamentals](http://senseis.xmp.net/?FirstFundamentals)** by [Robert Jasiek](http://senseis.xmp.net/?RobertJasiek)
- **[Opening Theory Made Easy](http://senseis.xmp.net/?OpeningTheoryMadeEasy)**( _Tsuyoku Naru Fuseki no Shintoku_) by [Otake Hideo](http://senseis.xmp.net/?OtakeHideo)
- [**Nie Weiping On Go**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?NieWeipingOnGo) _(The Art of Positional Judgement)_ by Chinese Pro [Nie Weiping](http://senseis.xmp.net/?NieWeiping)
- **[Positional Judgment High-Speed Game Analysis](http://senseis.xmp.net/?PositionalJudgmentHighSpeedGameAnalysis)** translated by Stuart Dowsey (original:: Japanese book by [Cho Chikun](http://senseis.xmp.net/?ChoChikun))
- [**Invincible – The Games of Shusaku**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?InvincibleTheGamesOfShusaku) translated by [John Power](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JohnPower)
- **[Train Like a Pro](http://senseis.xmp.net/?TrainLikeAPro)**(part 1 and 2) by 8 Pro Dan [Kim Sung-Rae](http://senseis.xmp.net/?KimSungRae)
- [**Kihon Fuseki Jiten**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?RinKaiHoFusekiDictionary) (known as [**Dictionary of Basic Fusekis**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?DictionaryOfBasicFuseki) (Vol. 1-4) edited by [Rin Kaiho](http://senseis.xmp.net/?RinKaiho)
- **[The Chinese Opening](http://senseis.xmp.net/?TheChineseOpening)**( _Kore ga Chuugoku-Ryuu Fuseki Da_) by Japanese [Kato Masao](http://senseis.xmp.net/?KatoMasao)
- [**Joseki / Volume 1: Fundamentals**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JosekiVolume1Fundamentals) / [**Volume 2: Strategy**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JosekiVolume2Strategy) written by [Robert Jasiek](http://senseis.xmp.net/?RobertJasiek)
- [**Ishida’s Joseki Dictionary**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?IshidasJosekiDictionary) an English translation by [John Power](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JohnPower) (original: [Ishida Yoshio](http://senseis.xmp.net/?IshidaYoshio)‘s [Kihon Joseki Jiten](http://senseis.xmp.net/?KihonJosekiJiten))
- [**Modern Joseki and Fuseki**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?ModernJosekiAndFusekiVol1) (Vol. 1 and 2) published by [Ishi Press](http://senseis.xmp.net/?IshiPress)
- [**The Middle Game of Go**](http://senseis.xmp.net/?TheMiddleGameOfGo) written by [Sakata Eio](http://senseis.xmp.net/?SakataEio)
- **[The Endgame – the book](http://senseis.xmp.net/?TheEndgameTheBook)** written by [Tomoko Ogawa](http://senseis.xmp.net/?TomokoOgawa) and [James Davies](http://senseis.xmp.net/?JamesDavies)
- BADUK CLASSIC Series No. 1: [**The Profound and Mysterious**](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/2014/08/04/baduk-classic-new-book-series-by-9pdan-cho-hyeyeon/) (Vol. 1-4) translated by Korena 9P Dan [Cho Hyeyeon](http://senseis.xmp.net/?ChoHyeYeon)
- BADUK CLASSIC Series No. 2: [**The ART of CLOSING – Guanzipu**](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/2014/12/13/baduk-classic-series-no-2-the-art-of-closing-guanzipu-vol-1-6-translated-by-9pdan-cho-hyeyeon/) (Vol. 1-6) translated by Korena 9P Dan [Cho Hyeyeon](http://senseis.xmp.net/?ChoHyeYeon)
- [**The Master of Haengma**](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/2014/10/19/two-korean-books-2009-about-haengma/) written by Korean [Baek Seong-ho](http://www.wbaduk.com/abaduk/abaduk_player_view.asp?gamer_no=164&n_code=101) and translated by [Diana Koszegi](http://senseis.xmp.net/?DianaKoszegi)
- **[This is Haengma](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/2014/10/19/two-korean-books-2009-about-haengma/)** written by 8 Pro Dan [Kim Sung-Rae](http://senseis.xmp.net/?KimSungRae).

- Some more you find in my Blog category “ [GO Books](https://mysanrensei.wordpress.com/category/go-books/)“

**What about to order Go books directly from stores of the leading nations (Korea, China and Japane) ?** – Today was announced on Facebook a [**new Japanese Go ebook store**](https://go-weiqi-baduk-ebook.stores.jp/#!/) with following 30 book titles (see covers).

The price of each single eBook (as PDF download) is **3,000 Japanese Yen** (= 21.3001 Euros / 25.0046 US $) with credit card payment (VISA, Master, AMEX).

**Would you buy these original Japanese books as PDF download ? – Do you know any of these books ? – Pls leave a comment about your own experiences… and check out the online store on your own [here](https://go-weiqi-baduk-ebook.stores.jp/#!/).**

